No hold at a break on an ultimate stop's end frame (2026-11-27, the break placement round; dropped)

The engine's breakHold (timeline/clock.ts) and the replay's breakStops (holds.ts) leave out a break inside an
ultimate's time stop; this counts the stop's end frame as inside it too (inUltimateStop, ULTIMATE_STOP_END_FRAMES = 1).
The case: 4d60e7fe92c2 56.29 s, Arcane's ultimate breaks at its frame 47, the stop's 47 frames just over (frame 1689 =
its end); Zhuang Fangyi's Sunderblade #7 at 56.36 s, 6 frames after #6 at 54.65 s across the 1.57 s stop, and Arcane's
combo event at 56.90 s (its 9-frame stop's end) both on time: no hold there (scripts/probes/stagger/ult-edge.ts lists
the breaks near an ultimate stop: only 4d60 and 04d401ad257e 458.25 s, a frame after its stop, are held at one under `ms`). Measured
(measure --variant clock.ts:ULTIMATE_STOP_END_FRAMES=0 against the tree with it, on top of break-hold-place
`moments`, which already moves 4d60's hold into the stop): development unchanged, hold-outs 1 mixed (plain −1, assumed
+1 with the rule). Dropped: one log's evidence, the replay already right there under `moments`, and an engine change
(simulated fights) for no development gain. Worth again if a second log shows a break at an ultimate's stop end.

